1
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,818
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:07,877
attained every treasure
that the world had to offer.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:12,666
Smiling, even as he stood upon the scaffold,
he issued a challenge to the world.

4
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,275
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:15,380
You can have it.

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,197
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

7
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,100
Now you just have to find it.

8
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:25,840
Now those who dare to dream hoist their
flags and sail into the great pirate era.

9
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,317
Don't be here, don't be here.

10
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,060
I'm late, I'm late.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,500
1, 2, 3, shine, you, we come!

12
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:43,517
Don't let your wall, break
up, roll up, roll up!

13
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:49,357
I'm going to go with a
sweep from the jump start.

14
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,940
If you're going to go without a world,

15
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:40,457
1 2 3 Shine 1 2 3 Shine

16
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:43,400
1 2 3 Shine 1 2 3 Shine

17
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,620
We go!

18
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:51,460
We go!

19
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,560
Brother, it's too hard to dig here.

20
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,697
Of course it is.

21
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:03,260
This island is all rocks and tree roots.

22
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:05,957
No, don't bury us.

23
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,100
We're victims too.

24
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,957
Please, I'll do anything you want.

25
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,960
Just let me live. Captain Luffy.

26
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:12,037
No, I mean Black.

27
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,720
He made us do this

28
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:18,157
Listen, I have a secret to share with you.

29
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,400
We didn't give a damn about going
to the new world with the Straw Hats

30
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,240
The reason we joined

31
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:30,597
Was so we could stab them
in the back and collect

32
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:33,739
their bounties without them
ever suspecting a thing?

33
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,960
Oh, I won't let my friend die! Oh, God!

34
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:46,580
Take that, bastard!

35
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,190
Huh?

36
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,040
Uh-oh.

37
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:54,420
That's weird. Whoa!

38
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:56,900
And sure,

39
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,257
your Straw Hat did look a little off,

40
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:02,634
but it had been two years,
so I didn't think much of it.

41
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:08,820
You lied without remorse, and deception
is a sin, one that you will be buried for.

42
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,960
Brother, how goes the grave?

43
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,780
I'm digging! I'm digging!

44
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:16,260
Sinners all, these poor fools.

45
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:21,160
Gods in heaven, please forgive them.

46
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:24,580
Grant them peace and death. Yes! No!

47
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:27,060
Peace, yes, but not death!

48
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:30,360
Still, it's not all bad, I suppose.

49
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,920
I did find the real Luffy.

50
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:38,057
I told you there wasn't
any choice in the matter.

51
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:39,316
What did you expect?

52
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,397
Dark King Rayleigh was there.

53
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,120
He's as strong as Kizaru.

54
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:47,166
Even with the pacifistas, we
couldn't so much as slow him down.

55
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:51,357
Unfortunately, the Caribou Brothers
escaped along with the rest of their crew.

56
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:54,617
It seems they took some of the
fake Straw Hats with them as well,

57
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,288
though I can't imagine why.

58
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,817
At any rate, we captured
most of the pirates,

59
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:02,397
even though the real Straw Hats
heavily damaged two of our pacifistas.

60
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:06,120
One of the units was the same
prototype they fought before.

61
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,957
Its strength hasn't changed
in the last two years.

62
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,440
That's bad news. For us.

63
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,637
I don't know what they've been up to,

64
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:18,426
but the Straw Hats are immeasurably
more dangerous than before.

65
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:22,757
Tell the Marines in the New World that
they have a new threat coming their way.

66
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:27,487
The Straw Hats have returned, and they're
stronger than we could have imagined.

67
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,240
A pity they had to take off so soon.

68
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,217
But I'm proud of them.

69
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,517
They're tough.

70
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,188
They're gonna do just fine!

71
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,420
You were watching?

72
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,240
Yes, I'm a big fan!

73
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:50,137
I know that smile, Ray.

74
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:51,740
What's on your mind?

75
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,130
Huh?

76
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,150
Ah

77
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,380
It's nothing, really.

78
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:00,920
Whoa! Oh!

79
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,537
Hey, that's a nice ship you got there.

80
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:06,397
Thanks, but it's not exactly mine.

81
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,897
Rather, I stole it after
my house burned down.

82
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:09,810
Oh, yeah?

83
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,135
And what's your name?

84
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,070
Rayleigh.

85
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,480
My name's Roger.

86
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:18,920
It's destiny meeting you, I say. Oh, yeah?

87
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:23,520
How about we team up and turn
this whole world upside down? Huh?

88
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,480
And I thought I drank too much.

89
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:30,497
I don't know who you are or what
you're selling, but I'm not interested.

90
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,410
Come on!

91
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:35,320
Before then, I never
believed much in fate.

92
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:38,800
But maybe nothing really
happens by accident.

93
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:43,100
We're just too blind to see all the signs.

94
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:46,700
Anyway, that hat found the right man.

95
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:50,060
So long as it sails,
I'll stay here, waiting.

96
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:53,940
Because I want to see a
new king before I die.

97
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:57,557
The surface is already so far away.

98
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,900
What a view!

99
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,017
I've been under before, but
portholes on a submarine?

100
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,620
They got nothing on this!

101
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,880
We're sinking! Sinking!

102
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,517
What if we get a leak?

103
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,012
This is freaking me out!

104
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:12,157
Yeah, it feels like we're
leaving the whole world behind.

105
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:14,040
It's eerie. No big deal.

106
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,917
I've done this like a
bajillion times before.

107
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:17,830
It's cool.

108
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:21,240
Nope, not pooping my pants at all here!

109
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,700
The ocean sure is awesome!

110
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,020
Look at that!

111
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:36,768
They really are trees, huh?

112
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:42,040
Wow, I totally forgot about that!

113
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:46,180
They're giant mangroves.

114
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,837
You can't tell when you're up top,

115
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:50,737
but it's sure quite a sight
to see from down here.

116
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:53,400
The majesty of nature is truly humbling!

117
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,717
Why, my eyes would be
popping out of my skull!

118
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:58,035
If I had any eyes to speak of, I mean.

119
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,860
Who cares? I've seen this.

120
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:03,680
Because you got on the
wrong ship! Shut up!

121
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:05,480
Don't ruin this for us!

122
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,920
These roots, they're beautiful.

123
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,458
And think about it.

124
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:13,215
They stretch all the way down
to the bottom of the sea.

125
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,500
Okay, you win.

126
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,980
Hey, Chopper, I think there's
something behind that tree. Huh?

127
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,130
Whoa!

128
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,360
It's huge!

129
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,257
Took us long enough to get here.

130
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:33,257
But whatever, it was worth the wait.

131
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:34,811
I wonder what comes next?

132
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,020
Oh, fishies!

133
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:38,440
I bet I didn't grab them!

134
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,160
I see.

135
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,777
These look pretty good, too.

136
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:42,690
Here goes.

137
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,600
That's not funny!

138
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,040
If you put that bubble and we all
die, I'm gonna kill you! Twice!

139
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:53,157
Nami, you know how the
coding works, right?

140
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:56,657
Can we get some basic tips before
another idiot flips out on us?

141
00:07:56,740 --> 00:08:00,920
Good point, okay Rayleigh gave me
a manual, but I can summarize it.

142
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,920
So listen closely, okay?

143
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,180
It's real!

144
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,820
I can die happy!

145
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:07,620
You're such a king!

146
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:10,020
You don't have to take us with you!

147
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,965
Who's flipping out now, idiot?

148
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,210
What?!

149
00:08:15,293 --> 00:08:17,980
His nosebleed shot out! I see.

150
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,987
It maintains its shape well.

151
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,437
You'd think that it would burst,

152
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,617
Especially considering
the immense amount of

153
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,397
water pressure the coating
must be exposed to.

154
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,310
How nice.

155
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:31,126
And I thought we'd all drown down
here, never to be seen again.

156
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,210
Salty!

157
00:08:33,293 --> 00:08:34,123
Get out of here!

158
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:38,840
Bright seawater, dammit!

159
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:40,260
Pull up for me!

160
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:55,297
Ah, gee, what the heck
happened to you back there?

161
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:58,917
I knew you were weak to pretty
girls, but this is a real liability.

162
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,588
You're supposed to be cool.

163
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,860
That poor man.

164
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:06,417
I can only imagine the horrors he must
have endured during the past two years.

165
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:10,857
Let's hope he lives long enough to see
the mermaids he was so looking forward to.

166
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:11,770
Uh,

167
00:09:11,853 --> 00:09:13,957
and let's also hope they aren't quite so

168
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,317
lovely that the sight of
them strikes him dead.

169
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:19,657
When we get there, we'll have
to ask for blood donations.

170
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:21,260
But they won't be human.

171
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,461
I hope fishmen have the
same kind of blood as him.

172
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:25,490
So,

173
00:09:25,573 --> 00:09:28,717
Sunny's coating has the same
properties as the bubbles on Sabaody,

174
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,897
meaning that objects or people can pass in

175
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:33,317
and out without causing
it any harm at all.

176
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,797
Spare me the bubble science!

177
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,400
We got a man down here!

178
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,420
Sanji aside, she's not wrong.

179
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,680
We saw this all over Sabaody.

180
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:44,697
It only stretches so far, then
allows an object to pass through.

181
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:48,957
So the good news is if we get
attacked by any nasty sea creatures,

182
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:53,511
We can still fire cannons at them just
like we would if we were above water!

183
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,880
Wait, so what would pop it?

184
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,460
Is it that durable?

185
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,397
It does fine with single objects,

186
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,797
but if too many things pass
through at once then it'll break.

187
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:06,700
Let's see like if a sea king clamps down
on the ship for example, that's bad.

188
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:19,577
Also the coating doesn't protect the
ship from anything except water so if

189
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:22,977
we crash into a rock or a trench and
the mast breaks or something like that

190
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:26,337
then the bubble could also burst so
it's not like we can just bounce around

191
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:30,237
down here still as long as we take the
usual precautions we should be fine.

192
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:33,577
I mean I'm sure Luffy will try to get
us all killed but what else is new.

193
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:35,737
So we're in clear.

194
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:36,897
After all, good.

195
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:40,397
Well, in theory at least.

196
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,357
But a lot of ships try
to make the trip to Fish

197
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,637
Man Island and over 70
percent of them sink.

198
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:48,417
We are so dead.

199
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:54,277
One Gum-Gum gatling and I bet I can
catch all the fish swimming out there.

200
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,737
Yeah, if I cut enough holes in this bubble
thing I bet I could catch even more.

201
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:00,637
Aren't you listening to Nami?

202
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,077
That's too many holes.

203
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,417
Our chances down here?

204
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,912
are bad enough as it is!

205
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:05,890
Oh, break your bones!

206
00:11:05,973 --> 00:11:06,803
Let's fix them!

207
00:11:06,886 --> 00:11:07,716
Let's break them again!

208
00:11:07,799 --> 00:11:08,629
No fair!

209
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,757
Haji said he'd show us the Fishman Island?

210
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,737
Like it was no big deal, And now
we're stuck in this death bubble!

211
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,420
slowly descending to our demise! Oh, yeah!

212
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,740
Lunch time!

213
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,837
They packed a bunch of food for me!

214
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:22,997
Since Sanji's sick, we should
have ourselves a Pikmin!

215
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,910
Yay!

216
00:11:23,993 --> 00:11:25,617
All that screaming made me hungry!

217
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:28,940
Oh, and I'm wasting away! Cool.

218
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:32,382
As long as Nami thinks
the ship will stay stable,

219
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,477
We don't have to steer it or
anything right now, do we?

220
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,390
Nope.

221
00:11:36,473 --> 00:11:39,577
We'll just be cruising on the sea
current till we get further down.

222
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:40,520
So, yeah.

223
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:43,037
I'm sure we'll have more
excitement a bit later.

224
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:46,337
But for the time being, we might as
well just kick back and take it easy.

225
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:49,357
Well, I wouldn't call this
taking it easy, exactly.

226
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:54,322
But there's something you guys should
probably know before we reach Fishman Island.

227
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:56,100
It's so much surprise!

228
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:59,060
You got all kinds of secrets, don't you?

229
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:00,877
Can you transform into a tank?

230
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:01,901
Oh, wait, maybe?

231
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,700
You've got laser guns!

232
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:04,960
Tell us, Robo-Pro!

233
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,680
Super-armored! Me.

234
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:16,060
Sorry, no new secrets.

235
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,800
Secrets inaccessible, Robo.

236
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:21,100
He speaks robot!

237
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,940
OK, I know robots are cool.

238
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:26,340
But listen up.

239
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:28,800
Or eat and listen, if you like.

240
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,740
Like Usopp said,

241
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,857
Hachi was supposed to show us the
way to Fishman Island himself,

242
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,660
but he got hurt real bad back on Sabo Odi.

243
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:40,195
He came down here ahead of
us to get medical treatment.

244
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:43,418
Anyway, it was the same
thing that happened to Duval.

245
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:47,944
Meaning, he was protecting the
Sunny from anyone who came for it.

246
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:52,957
Things got ugly about a year ago when the
Navy found out the ship was docked there.

247
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,864
Both him and Duval got
taken out in a big fight.

248
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:57,930
Huh?

249
00:12:58,013 --> 00:12:58,920
Wait, a year?

250
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:01,537
Then who was protecting
the Sunny after that?

251
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:04,060
We had one more secret ally.

252
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:06,640
If not really, then who?

253
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:10,560
Someone who separated us two
years ago, for better or worse.

254
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:12,460
The Warlord. Huh?

255
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:18,220
Turns out Bartholomew Kuma was
on our side the whole time.

256
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:19,860
A few days back.

257
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,157
When I made it to the Sunny,
I couldn't believe my eyes.

258
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,720
He was right there.

259
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:31,840
I've been waiting for you.

260
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:35,121
What the hell are you doing here?

261
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,220
Mission accomplished.

262
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:59,200
You saw for yourself, there wasn't
a single scratch on the Sunny.

263
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:02,080
Later, Rayleigh gave me the whole story.

264
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:05,137
I am a member of the Revolutionary Army.

265
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:09,377
If it's within my power, I want to
help the Straw Hats escape from here.

266
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:13,177
You guys probably knew that something
was up, but now we know the truth.

267
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:16,400
He saved the Sunny,
and he saved our lives.

268
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:21,159
And then, after we were
sent flying from the island,

269
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:25,337
Kuma paid Rayleigh a visit
and dropped another bombshell.

270
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,773
I don't have much time.

271
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,020
Not as myself.

272
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:33,780
The details are a little
sketchy, But evidently,

273
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,235
Kuma surrendered his body to the Navy.

274
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:40,618
They used him as an experiment and
replaced his body parts one by one.

275
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:42,957
By the time the War of
the Best rolled around,

276
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:46,120
his personality had been
completely erased. Wait,

277
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:50,577
he knew where he sent us, but he didn't
know what we'd do once we got there,

278
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:52,417
and that we would even make it back.

279
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:56,717
And you said his personality was taken
away, but he still protected the Sunny?

280
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:00,177
The guy who worked on him is
this dude named Dr. Vegapunk,

281
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,617
And Kuma must have made
a deal with him because

282
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:05,357
he programmed one final
mission into his brain.

283
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,537
Defend the Thousand Sunny
from any attackers until

284
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,444
the moment that a Straw
Hat returns to claim it.

285
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:15,657
So even though he's been reduced
to a living weapon with no memory,

286
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,897
he's been carrying out his own orders,

287
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:22,300
protecting our ship for the past
two years to fulfill his last wish.

288
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,580
But why?

289
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,160
He barely knew us.

290
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:28,160
I mean, why'd it matter
to him? I don't know.

291
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:29,817
Maybe it's cause of Luffy.

292
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:32,397
You said Kuma was part of
the Revolutionary Army,

293
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:35,539
and Luffy's dad was the
leader of those guys, right?

294
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:37,844
I don't know much about my dad,

295
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,737
but it seems like that robot
bear dude was a good guy,

296
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:43,237
so he can't be too bad if they're friends.

297
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,150
Kuma.

298
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,840
The bottom line is,

299
00:15:46,020 --> 00:15:49,757
our survival and all the things we
accomplished in the past two years,

300
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:50,670
we owe to him.

301
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,905
Whatever his reason was,
we should be grateful.

302
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,937
And we may never find out the truth,

303
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:58,797
because it's not like we can ask
him to explain himself anymore.

304
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:02,677
all we can do now is
honor his memory and know

305
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:05,289
that Bartholomew Kuma
was our greatest ally

306
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,697
until he took his last breath as a human.

307
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:11,309
Unfortunately, we'll
never be able to thank

308
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:15,597
him since he'll just be a weapon and
likely our enemy the next time we meet.

309
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,268
That's all I wanted to say.

310
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,677
Kind of a lot to work through
all at once, isn't it?

311
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,590
Someday.

312
00:16:20,673 --> 00:16:23,037
I hope we can at least find
out the rest of the story.

313
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:24,380
Kuma saved us, huh?

314
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:27,577
Oh, you're awake. Good. Have some lunch.

315
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:29,140
It's from Amazon Lily.

316
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,980
Oh, Amazon Lily.

317
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,577
The island with all the women.

318
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,177
Of course that's where he sent you.

319
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,197
Do you know where I was
these past two years?

320
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:39,397
Because I'm kind of thinking Kuma's
not such a good friend after all.

321
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:42,457
In fact, if he were here right now,
I'd like to kick his metal face in!

322
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:43,481
Now, now, Sanji.

323
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,157
We've all had our share of troubles.

324
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,537
Before I became a pop music
sensation, I was trapped in a cage.

325
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:51,497
Still, the only thing that matters
now is the voyage awaiting us.

326
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:52,537
You don't know, man!

327
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,032
You don't know anything!

328
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,157
Straight ahead!

329
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,200
Brother, look!

330
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:57,920
It's them! I know.

331
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,257
Like you said, they're straight ahead.

332
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:01,516
You think I'm blind?

333
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:06,052
Looks like we'll be sailing
with the Straw Hats after all.

334
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:08,440
Wow, how far down are we?

335
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:11,760
I don't know, but it's
getting darker and darker.

336
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:14,397
We passed the photic zone,

337
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,677
and it looks like we're around
the bottom of the aphotic zone.

338
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:19,995
About a thousand meters, give or take.

339
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:24,500
It's quiet, and the sunny
itself feels oddly still.

340
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,360
It's almost like floating in the sky

341
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:40,380
Wait a sec, what is that thing a fish?

342
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:42,540
No, are you ready?

343
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,820
We only get one shot at this

344
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:50,117
Before you say anything, I
know what you're thinking.

345
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,297
Just shoot them and they'll all drown.

346
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,897
They're wanted dead or alive, after all.

347
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:56,457
So why not let them die?

348
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:58,517
Well, that would do it all.

349
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:01,017
Because the Navy wouldn't
know who killed them.

350
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:04,877
We have to deliver their heads
personally on a silver platter.

351
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:06,697
Then they will fear us.

352
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:09,757
The whole world will do our strength.

353
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:12,937
We'll take them out before they suspect.

354
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:19,120
My big smiling face is the last thing
they'll see before they die! Yes, sir!

355
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:20,920
Uh, right there!

356
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:27,040
Hey, you guys, there's a ship-looking
thing coming our way. What? You sure?

357
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,097
Why don't you come look for yourself?

358
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,010
Charge!

359
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:40,000
It's a pilot ship!

360
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,757
They're ramming straight into us!

361
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:43,460
Go away, you morons!

362
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,640
You're going to make us all drown!

363
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,317
They're not trying to break our ship.

364
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,988
They're trying to board it!

365
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:56,780
Dummies, who are they?

366
00:18:58,740 --> 00:18:59,570
Run!

367
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,820
Hard to board, now!

368
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,080
Attack them, CJ!

369
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:17,240
Oh, tenacious, aren't they? That sound...

370
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,426
They don't know when to quit.

371
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,640
Who are these guys after?

372
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:29,440
The bubble's about to pop!

373
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,920
Keep it up, sea cow! Yeah!

374
00:19:32,660 --> 00:19:33,997
You think they want to board the ship?

375
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:34,910
Sea cow?

376
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:37,921
I know that noise from somewhere.

377
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,800
The two bubbles are touching!

378
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:45,680
This is a big moment, brother! Good!

379
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,960
Is everybody ready?

380
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:49,410
Yeah!

381
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:50,840
Mama, it's me!

382
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,977
We've met before!

383
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,157
You're from the Arlong Pirates, right?

384
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,900
Do you remember me? Nami!

385
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:58,900
I was at Arlong Park!

386
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:04,340
Hey, Luffy, doesn't that
thing look kind of familiar?

387
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:05,820
I don't know.

388
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,020
Dump-pump pistol!

389
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:17,520
Let's pay our new friends
a visit, shall we?

390
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:22,280
Hey, that guy's up to something!

391
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,658
Stay out of my car!

392
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:25,936
Guess he's looking for a fight, then.

393
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:30,500
There's no time to waste!

394
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,940
Follow my lead!

395
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:34,950
Fools!

396
00:20:35,033 --> 00:20:36,597
They're completely dumbfounded.

397
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:39,937
If they're gonna sit there
catching flies Then we'll strike

398
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:44,820
while the iron is hot We'll
smite this entire crew Right now

399
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:47,780
For glory

400
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:53,720
Come along men We'll make
the beggars for mercy?

401
00:20:59,220 --> 00:21:01,657
What's wrong Skull? Don't panic.

402
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:02,997
That's not good.

403
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:05,727
We left Captain Tribe
on the ship back there.

404
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,197
Now it's time for a little greeting!

405
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:14,997
Fire the Gatling gun!

406
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:17,800
Men, shower them in bullets!

407
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:21,057
I want every last one of them dead!

408
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,817
Send these Straw Hats.

409
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,000
THE HELL!

410
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,290
Huh?

411
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,350
No! Wait!

412
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,537
You're not going to throw
me into the water, are you?

413
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:45,077
Please don't do that to me, my friend!

414
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:46,037
I'm begging you!

415
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:46,950
Come on!

416
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:48,997
You're a reasonable fellow, are you not?

417
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:51,157
By the way, you're very good-looking!

418
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:55,299
I'm sure someone like you understands
the value of human life, right?

419
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:56,670
Emphasize!

420
00:21:56,753 --> 00:21:58,120
The gods are watching!

421
00:21:58,320 --> 00:21:59,849
You'll be judged for this!

422
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:02,714
Oh, make up your freaking mind already!

423
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:06,997
Weren't you just about to fire your Gatling
gun and blast us all to kingdom come?

424
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,240
Me? No!

425
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:11,780
I was just, uh, I was just joking around!

426
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:13,000
I ain't laughing.

427
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,460
Anyway, tell me.

428
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:18,177
I know you're the captain of
that ship, but what's your name?

429
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:19,620
That's Roro no Azoro!

430
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,557
Uh, don't be ridiculous.

431
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,897
What in the world makes you
think I would be the captain?

432
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:26,660
I'm, uh, oh!

433
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,400
Those ruffians were keeping
me as a, a slave! That's it!

434
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,080
Boy, ooh, glad that's over!

435
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:34,860
Say, how's this?

436
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:38,417
Do you think I could stay on this nice
ship with you all for a little while?

437
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:39,680
Huh? Please?

438
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:43,160
Wow, I feel kind of sorry
for this poor loser.

439
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,700
He's obviously lying! Are you crazy?

440
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:47,680
What? Seriously?

441
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,793
Hey, I have a question.

442
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:52,897
Where'd that giant sea cow
pulling your ship come from?

443
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:53,810
Hello.

444
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,080
Oh, my.

445
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,580
Who's this vixen?

446
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:02,880
I take it you're the famous cat burglar.

447
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,017
Oh, watch it, pal.

448
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:08,057
Nobody's allowed to drool over our
beautiful navigator except for me.

449
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:09,060
Don't worry.

450
00:23:10,340 --> 00:23:11,458
You're perfectly...

451
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,960
Hey, it's getting really old.

452
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:16,040
Cut it out.

453
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,130
The sea cow?

454
00:23:17,213 --> 00:23:18,140
Who knows?

455
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:20,977
I just happened to catch it
out in the ocean somewhere.

456
00:23:21,060 --> 00:23:22,413
When you're underwater,

457
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:27,013
having a sea monster pull your ship
is the mark of an experienced captain.

458
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:28,880
Huh? Awesome!

459
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:33,180
Stop it, sea cow!

460
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,660
What's the problem?

461
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:36,370
Brother!

462
00:23:36,453 --> 00:23:38,260
We're on our way to rescue you!

463
00:23:38,820 --> 00:23:41,000
I'm gonna find a sea monster, too!

464
00:23:42,080 --> 00:23:44,840
What crazy ideas are
you hatching now, Luffy?

465
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:50,140
We should try to rehabilitate him
with something a little less sexy.

466
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:51,070
Hey, Nami,

467
00:23:51,153 --> 00:23:54,937
the direction we're taking isn't exactly
the same way the Log Pose is pointing.

468
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:56,320
Oh, no problem.

469
00:23:56,720 --> 00:24:00,661
The correct course is technically
southwest, so we're in the clear.

470
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:02,717
Yeah, but if we went in a straight line,

471
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:05,257
we could get there a whole
lot faster, couldn't we?

472
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:08,377
Well, if you go straight, you risk
getting swept away in a sea current.

473
00:24:08,460 --> 00:24:12,657
And if that should happen, you might run
into an underwater mountain or a volcano,

474
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:13,570
see?

475
00:24:13,653 --> 00:24:14,483
That's why.

476
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:15,480
Huh? Yikes!

477
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:17,280
I'm with you on this one.

478
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:19,937
Yeah, but I thought all the
currents here were dangerous.

479
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:21,877
It is the Grand Line, after all.

480
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:24,717
So are you saying that some
of them are actually stable?

481
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:26,060
Well, this one is.

482
00:24:26,580 --> 00:24:27,720
That should do it.

483
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,780
Now you stay put. Hey!

484
00:24:30,100 --> 00:24:32,357
It's gonna start getting
colder from here on out,

485
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:34,377
so make sure you put
on a coat or something.

486
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:35,557
You bring up a good point.

487
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:38,640
I'm already starting to
feel goosebumps on my skin.

488
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:40,437
Well, except for I...

489
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,461
You don't have any skin
because you're a skeleton.

490
00:24:45,900 --> 00:24:48,665
Chopper, skull jokes are
the only thing I have.

491
00:24:48,860 --> 00:24:50,978
Please don't take that away from me.

492
00:24:51,280 --> 00:24:53,980
We're going somewhere
cold, not the deep sea.

493
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:57,117
Don't you guys know the
water's cold in the deep sea?

494
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,497
It's just like a bathtub.

495
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:01,227
Hot water rises and cold
sinks to the bottom.

496
00:25:01,540 --> 00:25:02,420
Oh, does it?

497
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:05,020
It won't take very many baths. Aha,

498
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:07,717
because heat rises and
there's not much sunlight,

499
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:10,057
so there's nothing to
heat the water down here.

500
00:25:10,140 --> 00:25:13,677
The temperature's not the only thing
that's different at the bottom.

501
00:25:13,760 --> 00:25:16,997
you're not still depressed
are you once we move

502
00:25:17,080 --> 00:25:19,877
down we'll find something
called deep currents

503
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:22,097
you don't run into them terribly often but

504
00:25:22,180 --> 00:25:25,297
they're much larger than
the regular currents also

505
00:25:25,380 --> 00:25:27,237
they're quite unique in that their flow is

506
00:25:27,320 --> 00:25:29,317
completely independent of
what you see closer to the

507
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,697
surface currents under
the currents and you even

508
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,900
have a diagram huh you
sure do know a lot of stuff

509
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:39,197
that's because I'm so
old not only that but

